			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b1ad6273-a5c7-4a68-b019-bad9bb2e2197")
	)
	(text_box "Note: when DIA_EN is high and EN is low, the device will perform open-load detection. An unloaded output will read ~21 V on a multimeter for 24 V input. However, this is a high-impedance output (~1 MΩ) and will drop to zero for any load - the switch is still OFF. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 109.22 101.6 0)
		(size 59.69 11.43)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type dot)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c63dfa11-33f8-43d1-8bf0-13af301f1e79")
	)
	(text_box "> For current sensing I range 0 - 30 A, I_{SNSI} current range is 0 - 6.522 mA. \n  (from datasheet, worst-case current limit range is 12.8 - 27.8 A (nominally 20 A))\n> For thermal sensing range -40 - 150 °C, I_{SNST} current range is 0 - 2.25 mA. \n  (values obtained from datasheet table, operating temp range is -40 - 125 °C)\n> For voltage sensing range 0 - 40 V, I_{SNSV} current range is 0 - 3.468 mA. \n  (values obtained from datasheet table, operating voltage range is 8 - 36 V, with max long transient 40 V)\n\nWhen the device is faulted, SNS will output I_{SNSFH} (6.9 mA nom, 7.6 mA max) and the ~{ST} pin will be pulled low.\n\nAs the ADC full-scale voltage is 3.3 V, target a SNS voltage range of 0 - 3 V (to provide some buffer).\nResistor value is selected to be R_{SNS} = 392 Ω (ideally 394.737 Ω), then...\nFault range: 0 - 2.9792 V\nCurrent sensing range: 0 - 2.568 V\nThermal sensing range: 0 - 0.882 V (consider using PGA)\nVoltage sensing range: 0 - 1.359 V (consider using PGA)\n\nPreferably a 1% tolerance resistor. (Maximum voltage with worst-case resistor 3.009 V)\nConsider measuring each resistor and populating its precise value in code to maximize sensing accuracy.\n\nWhen EN is low and DIA_EN is high, the device will perform open-load detection and output I_{SNSFH} if detected.\n\nIt is recommended for the software to take multiple samples and use a median.\n\nThe sensitivity of current measurements of this device is 85.22 mV/A."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 152.4 0)
		(size 88.9 43.18)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c7cc483e-26ba-4e31-8ffc-82d2258ba99a")
	)
	(text_box "HSS DIAGNOSTICS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 133.35 0)
		(size 88.9 3.81)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(thickness 0.4)
				(bold yes)
				(italic yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cc62ab1a-1eed-43fc-9175-d2b96dad1d63")
	)
	(text_box "Current sensor reading:\nI_{sense} = ((V_{out} - V_{QVO})/S = (V_{out} - 1.65)/0.132 [A]\n\nFor the current sense range of -10 A to 10 A, the output voltage range is 0.33 - 2.97 V. \n\nFor this application's current range of 0 A to 8 A (SMD fuse value), the output voltage range is 1.65 - 2.706 V.\nWith ADCIN- set to 1.65 V, this is within the ADS131M08-Q1 ADC's input limit of 1.2 V differential (max: 1.056 V) and -1.3 to 3.3 V absolute. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 105.41 142.24 0)
		(size 67.31 53.34)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
